The orchard theme's face (~/.config/themes/orchard/ and orchard-dark/).

Inter -- the UI face (theme.conf font=): the bar, the toolbox, the popup
    panels, the launcher, wofi, mako, Nautilus, the LLM chat, mpv's OSD.
    By Rasmus Andersson and the Inter Project Authors
    (https://github.com/rsms/inter), version 4.1. A neo-grotesk drawn for
    computer screens -- a tall x-height, open apertures, tabular figures on
    "tnum" -- and the nearest open face to the system UI sans of the desktop
    this theme is modelled on. That face itself (Apple's San Francisco) is
    NOT used and never downloaded: its licence allows it only on Apple
    hardware. Fedora's Adwaita Sans is GNOME's own fork of Inter and is
    already installed, so every stack reads "Inter, Adwaita Sans, IBM Plex
    Sans": if this folder ever goes missing the theme looks almost the same.
    Variable: one wght axis, 100-900, so every weight the stylesheets ask
    for (300 the search field, 400 body, 500 bar items, 600 headings, 700
    the focused app's title) is an exact instance, and the Italic is its own
    variable file.
    Family name: the variable files are "Inter Variable", not "Inter" (the
    name of the static cuts, Inter.ttc, which is not installed). The alias
    in ~/.config/fontconfig/conf.d/60-inter-family.conf maps "Inter" onto
    "Inter Variable" (fc-match "Inter" printed Noto Sans before it).
    Files:  InterVariable.ttf  InterVariable-Italic.ttf
    Source: https://github.com/rsms/inter/releases/tag/v4.1
            https://github.com/rsms/inter/releases/download/v4.1/Inter-4.1.zip
            (sha256 9883fdd4a49d4fb66bd8177ba6625ef9a64aa45899767dde3d36aa425756b11e)
            the two .ttf files and LICENSE.txt taken from the zip's top
            level, unmodified.

Licence: SIL Open Font License 1.1 (OFL-1.1), LICENSE.txt here (copyright
(c) 2016 The Inter Project Authors): free to use, bundle and redistribute,
not to sell on its own; the licence travels with the files. No file was
modified.

The terminal face is NOT here: Adwaita Mono (Fedora's adwaita-mono-fonts,
OFL; GNOME's build of Iosevka) is installed system-wide and has a Bold,
which COSMIC Terminal needs (theme.py check confirms it).

Installed by copying into this folder and
    fc-cache -f ~/.local/share/fonts
then checked with `fc-match Inter:semibold`: InterVariable.ttf "Inter
Variable" "SemiBold". If it is missing: download the zip again from the URL
above, check its sha256, copy the three files here and rerun fc-cache.

